**Setup.** Factor $4032 = 2^6 \cdot 3^2 \cdot 7$. If $n = \prod p_i^{a_i}$, then $d(n) = \prod(a_i+1) = 16$ and $\sigma(n) = \prod \frac{p_i^{a_i+1}-1}{p_i-1} = 4032$.

